    "N1200"
  ],
  "vendor_website": "novus.com.br",
  "description": "Universal PID process controller with ramp and soak, four alarms and optional RS485 Modbus RTU: PV, setpoints, output power, status, PID, input, alarm, I/O and serial settings",
  "revision": 1,
  "revised": "2026-11-26",
  "firmware": "Communication protocol V1.0x",
  "source": "Novus N1200 communication protocol V10x",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "N1200 Communication Protocol",
      "version": "V10x",
      "url": "https://github.com/user-attachments/files/35246288/doc.1.pdf",
      "note": "register table and tables 2 and 3",
      "accessed": "2026-11-26",
      "sha256": "9f9c83f4d2c655756c847faf37c073f82c6ae4e69654859a4dfb0d37d40708b1"
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Modbus RTU needs the optional RS485 interface. Functions 03, 05, 06 and 16; writes with address 0 are broadcast.",
    "8 data bits, 1 stop bit, no, even or odd parity. The document gives no factory address, baud rate or parity: check the controller; 9600 bit/s without parity is assumed here.",
    "Every register is a signed 16-bit value. Registers 12 and up can be read and written; most registers below 12 are read-only.",
    "Process value, setpoints, limits, offset and alarm setpoints are integers in display units with the decimals of register 30; a temperature is read multiplied by 10.",
    "A write outside the allowed range is not refused: the controller stores the nearest limit and returns it.",
    "The document lists speeds up to 115200 bit/s but gives codes 0 to 4 (1200 to 19200) for register 45.",
    "The ramp and soak programs (registers 100 to 699: events, tolerances, links, times and setpoints of programs 1 to 20) and the calibration registers are not listed.",
    "Written from the manufacturer's document; not tested on a device."
  ],
  "protocol": "rtu",
  "unit_id": 1,
  "baudrate": 9600,
  "databits": 8,
  "parity": "N",
  "stopbits": 1,
  "byte_order": "big",
  "word_order": "big",
  "address_base": 0,
  "x_status": "official",
